      {
        "id": 229921,
        "name": "drkrash1969",
        "username": "drkrash1969",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/eada6e/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-03-07T14:15:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I've only listened to the 1st 5 episodes of Season 1...all this week.</p>\n<p>My understanding is that a bonus must be declared before the roll, and generally the bonus is going to be applied to the result (because only one die applies).</p>\n<p>If 2 dice are used for the result, it then seemed that the results are determined first (max-mid-min) and then the bonus is applied to one of them.</p>\n<p>If I'm right in my memory, that should be more clearly specified in the rules.&nbsp; I don't think it would make a difference very often, but I think it matters if ties are rolled.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:04:47.627Z",
