        "raw": "<p>I've only listened to the 1st 5 episodes of Season 1...all this week.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>My understanding is that a bonus must be declared before the roll, and generally the bonus is going to be applied to the result (because only one die applies).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If 2 dice are used for the result, it then seemed that the results are determined first (max-mid-min) and then the bonus is applied to one of them.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If I'm right in my memory, that should be more clearly specified in the rules.&nbsp; I don't think it would make a difference very often, but I think it matters if ties are rolled.</p>",
